		<title type="html"><![CDATA[osgBullet v2.0 now available (release notes, video)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=26127#p26127"><![CDATA[
<a href="http://code.google.com/p/osgbullet/" class="postlink">osgBullet v2.0</a> is now available!<br><br>osgBullet is a set of software tools for applications that use both <a href="http://www.openscenegraph.org" class="postlink">OpenSceneGraph (OSG)</a> and Bullet. Like OSG and Bullet, osgBullet is cross-platform C++ F/OSS, and available for use under LGPL. osgBullet was the recipient of a 2010 R&amp;D 100 award.<br><br>v2.0 is the first major revision to osgBullet since its inception, and features a reorganized library structure, new osgGA-based event handlers for mouse interaction with scene elements, complete Doxygen documentation, and a cleaner, easier-to-use API. Full <a href="http://code.google.com/p/osgbullet/wiki/ReleaseRoadmap#v2.0" class="postlink">release notes</a> are at the Google Code project page.<br><br>Watch <a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fr3wDGfZX4g&amp;feature=youtu.be" class="postlink">this video</a> to see some of osgBullet's examples in action.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2485">PaulMartz</a> — Tue Nov 08, 2011 3:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
